From 712827bcb7a57a56e503cbd172fd88425f71c478 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 02:07:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/36] docs: correct PORTING-NOTES.md for the GpgMe++ Qt4
 scope fix

Removes the now-wrong claims that src/Cryptography/GpgMe++ is Qt5-only
and that WITH_CRYPTO_MESSAGES=OFF is required for Qt4, and records the
26c0cf6a fix and its caveat (Qt4-side Gpgmepp/QGpgme CMake target names
are an informed guess pending a real WITH_GPGMEPP=ON Qt4 build).
---
 PORTING-NOTES.md | 51 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 43 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/PORTING-NOTES.md b/PORTING-NOTES.md
index a82abc7f..126c60f4 100644
--- a/PORTING-NOTES.md
+++ b/PORTING-NOTES.md
@@ -36,9 +36,11 @@ verification bullet 3) before trusting this branch.
    option (default ON), Qt4 module detection (`QtCore QtGui QtNetwork QtSql
    QtWebKit QtSvg`, `QtDBus`/`QtTest` conditionally), external `QtMimeTypes`
    (`devel/qt4-mimetypes`) wired via `pkg_check_modules` with a
-   `find_path`/`find_library` fallback, `WITH_CRYPTO_MESSAGES` made to depend
-   on `WITH_QT5` (GpgME++'s Qt integration is Qt5-only), translations
+   `find_path`/`find_library` fallback, translations
    (`Qt5LinguistForTrojita`) guarded to the Qt5 branch only.
+   `WITH_CRYPTO_MESSAGES` was originally made to depend on `WITH_QT5` here
+   under the assumption that GpgME++'s Qt integration was Qt5-only — that
+   assumption was wrong and was corrected later, see `26c0cf6a` below.
 2. **Ifdef restoration** (`436551e4`) — `git revert -n af84b80c` +
    `git revert -n e76c8774`, resolved against v0.7's current code (~20 files
    had real conflicts from v0.7 refactors: async `PasswordDialog`, the
@@ -107,9 +109,35 @@ in the static-analysis approach above, not just isolated bugs:
   `disconnect()` a signal — replaced with the classic 4-argument
   `disconnect(sender, SIGNAL, receiver, SLOT)`, which needs no `#if` guard
   since the connect side already uses `SIGNAL()`/`SLOT()` strings.
-  `GpgMe++.h` has the identical `QMetaObject::Connection` pattern but
-  **is** legitimately out of scope, since `GpgMe++.cpp` only enters the
-  build when `WITH_GPGMEPP` is ON.
+  `GpgMe++.h` has the identical `QMetaObject::Connection` pattern; it was
+  initially left alone here on the assumption that `GpgMe++.cpp`/real GPG
+  verification was legitimately Qt5-only and out of scope, since it only
+  enters the build when `WITH_GPGMEPP` is ON — see the next item, that
+  assumption was also wrong and was corrected immediately after.
+- **`src/Cryptography/GpgMe++.{h,cpp}` and the `WITH_GPGMEPP` cmake
+  detection** (`26c0cf6a`) — a second, related scope correction, this time
+  caught before a build error (the user pointed out the mistake directly):
+  GpgME++'s actual C++/Qt bindings are not Qt5-tied at all. What *is*
+  Qt5-only is `KF5Gpgmepp`, the specific CMake package used to find it — a
+  KDE Frameworks 5 package, always built against Qt5 by definition. Upstream
+  gpgme (not KDE) ships its own Qt-version-agnostic CMake package
+  (`Gpgmepp`, confirmed present as `<prefix>/lib/cmake/Gpgmepp/` plus a
+  `gpgmepp.pc` on the target MacPorts environment) and a separate `qgpgme`
+  library for the Qt integration bits, built against whichever Qt version
+  gpgme itself was configured for. Fixed: `WITH_QT5` dropped from
+  `WITH_CRYPTO_MESSAGES`'s cmake dependency list; the Qt4 branch now calls
+  `find_package(Gpgmepp)` instead of `find_package(KF5Gpgmepp)` and links
+  against `Gpgmepp::Gpgmepp`/`Gpgmepp::QGpgme` instead of
+  `KF5::Gpgmepp`/`KF5::QGpgme`; `GpgMe++.h`/`.cpp` got the same
+  `QMetaObject::Connection` → classic 4-argument `disconnect()` fix as
+  `MessageModel` above (3 call sites, all using the `m_sourceIndex` member
+  as the disconnect-time sender since it holds the same model as the
+  connect-time `sourceItemIndex` parameter). **The exact Qt4-side CMake
+  target names are an informed guess, not verified against a real
+  build** — `WITH_GPGMEPP` stays `OFF`/`AUTO` by default so this doesn't
+  affect anyone not opting in; whoever first builds with
+  `-DWITH_GPGMEPP=ON` on Qt4 should expect to adjust the target names in
+  the two comments flagging them in `CMakeLists.txt` if they don't match.
 - **Lesson for whoever continues iterating on build errors**: treat every
   compiler error as a prompt to grep-sweep for siblings of the same class
   of gap (a missed macro/pattern tends to have 2-8 siblings, as
@@ -181,7 +209,6 @@ depends_lib-append  port:qt4-mimetypes
 configure.args-append \
     -DWITH_QT5=OFF \
     -DWITH_SHARED_PLUGINS=OFF \
-    -DWITH_CRYPTO_MESSAGES=OFF \
     -DWITH_DBUS=OFF \
     -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PLUGIN_DIR=${prefix}/lib/trojita
 ```
@@ -192,8 +219,16 @@ Notes on these flags:
   this is what silently broke the v0.6 port (every diagnostic in
   `PluginManager.cpp` is behind `#ifdef PLUGIN_DEBUG`, so the original
   failure mode was "cannot find storage backend" with no further detail).
-- `WITH_CRYPTO_MESSAGES=OFF` is required, not optional, for the Qt4 build —
-  the cmake option now depends on `WITH_QT5`.
+- `WITH_CRYPTO_MESSAGES` is *not* forced off — unlike an earlier version of
+  this document claimed, it is not actually tied to `WITH_QT5`; whether it
+  ends up ON depends only on `WITH_MIMETIC`/`WITH_GPGMEPP` (both `AUTO` by
+  default, i.e. based on whether those libraries are found). Pass
+  `-DWITH_GPGMEPP=OFF` explicitly here if you want to keep real crypto
+  verification disabled for now (this is what the user's build has been
+  doing while iterating on the rest of the port) — see the "Fixes found
+  only by an actual Qt4 compile" section above for the caveat that the Qt4
+  `Gpgmepp`/`qgpgme` CMake target names haven't been verified against a
+  real build yet.
 - `WITH_QTKEYCHAIN_PLUGIN` is left at its default (`AUTO`) above; turn it ON
   explicitly if/when the target ports tree's qt4 qtkeychain is confirmed
   present and working — the Qt4 code path for this plugin was kept intact.
